            <p>In a world where everyone uses different devices, operating systems, and software versions, the <strong>Portable Document Format (PDF)</strong> is the universal language of business. Created by Adobe in the early 90s, its primary goal was "fidelity"—the promise that a document will look exactly the same on a screen in Tokyo as it does on a printer in New York.</p>
            
